      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, verified USM source, commit-pinned reproduction, CREATE2 deployment trace, historical runtime, and balances. The trace sends 11,579.978354608392803524 ETH to USM.fund, then makes 64 defund calls against the same onchain oracle result; the redemptions repay the flash loan and leave exactly 70.830977367697708372 ETH, matching USM's balance decrease from 132.588942983107019337 ETH to 61.757965615409310965 ETH. The defect-bearing calls execute directly at 0x2a7fff44c19f39468064ab5e5c304de01d591675. The EIP-2470 singleton deployer created that 22,589-byte runtime with CREATE2 at block 13390185; its hash is 0xd00517110af8636a194a019b7b343c8fc9019116ed2c07a93f214e961ffd70e9 both at deployment and immediately before exploit block 25716150, and explorer metadata identifies it as a non-proxy."
